<sys:String x:Key="GuideInstructions">Choose manual/custom partitioning in the native installer. Match the disk by model, capacity and partition UUIDs; lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,SERIAL,PARTUUID can help. Create an ext4 root partition mounted at / only inside the reserved region. Keep the installer data partition intact. Use the newly created 512 MiB FAT32 EFI partition for /boot/efi without reformatting it. ORCHESTER preserves that partition if the installed Linux bootloader uses it. Avoid encrypted/LVM roots if automatic read-back verification is required.</sys:String>
